-- NOT a drop-in file. These are the lines to ADD to the bottom of the stock
-- Quattro ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua, below its require() block.
--
-- Do NOT overwrite the shipped hyprland.lua — it contains the bootstrap
-- dofile() and the default require chain that everything else depends on.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- NVIDIA environment
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Ported from the top of your 3.8.4 hyprland.conf.
-- Hardware: NVIDIA RTX 3080 (driver 610.43.03) + AMD Raphael iGPU — hybrid.

hl.env("LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME", "nvidia")
hl.env("GBM_BACKEND", "nvidia-drm")
hl.env("__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME", "nvidia")

-- WLR_NO_HARDWARE_CURSORS is a legacy wlroots variable. Hyprland has its own
-- `cursor:no_hardware_cursors` setting and hasn't been wlroots-based for a long
-- time, so this is very likely dead weight carried forward from an old guide.
-- Your 3.8.4 line also used `env = NAME=VALUE` rather than Hyprland's
-- `env = NAME,VALUE` form.
--
-- Try WITHOUT it first after upgrading. If you get cursor flicker or an
-- invisible cursor, use the modern setting instead of the env var:
--   hl.config({ cursor = { no_hardware_cursors = true } })
-- hl.env("WLR_NO_HARDWARE_CURSORS", "1")

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ⚠️  DO NOT USE `omarchy toggle hybrid gpu` ON THIS MACHINE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- It is a LAPTOP feature. Its own summary line reads:
--   "Toggle dedicated vs integrated GPU mode via supergfxd
--    (for hybrid gpu laptops, like Asus G14)."
-- It drives supergfxd/supergfxctl — the asus-linux stack for muxless laptops
-- that power the dGPU down to save battery. It has no desktop use case.
--
-- It WILL still be offered to you. The gate is `omarchy-hw-hybrid-gpu`, which
-- with supergfxctl absent falls back to:
--   lspci | grep -cE 'VGA|3D|Display' >= 2
-- This desktop has 2 (RTX 3080 at 01:00.0 + AMD Raphael iGPU at 11:00.0), so
-- the toggle appears under Trigger > Hardware (SUPER+CTRL+H).
--
-- Choosing "Use only integrated GPU and reboot?" would be a BLACK SCREEN:
--   card2 (RTX 3080): DP-6 connected, HDMI-A-2 connected   <- both displays
--   card1 (AMD iGPU): DP-1, DP-2, DP-3, HDMI-A-1 ALL disconnected
-- Nothing is plugged into the motherboard video outputs, so an iGPU-only boot
-- has no display to drive. It also installs supergfxctl, writes
-- /etc/supergfxd.conf, and enables the supergfxd service as a side effect.
--
-- Everything already goes through the 3080. Keep the env vars above; ignore
-- the toggle.

